    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://youtu.be/drgmH5MBfPQ?si=tqusUbu3EKLcLf8_  THE BRITISH COMEDIAN TURNED CANADIAN, LIVE ON STAGE IN VICTORIA, PEI FOR THE VERY FIRST TIME!  This is it! James Mullinger’s first ever live stand-up comedy show at the beautiful Victoria Playhouse. Come and see Atlantic Canada’s biggest cheerleader doing what he does best! Live stand-up comedy at the Playhouse. 90 mins of stand-up comedy featuring James Mullinger at his very best!  12+ Recommended as there may be some strong language.  James Mullinger was one of the UK’s hardest working comedians and the Comedy Editor for GQ magazine when he moved to New Brunswick in 2014. Since his arrival, he has taken the country by storm. He has sold out shows across the country, made appearances on CBC’s The Debaters, movies, television shows, festivals, award shows and stand-up specials… he’s done it all. In May 2022, James Mullinger’s autobiography Brit Happens – Living the Canadian Dream was released to rave reviews and quickly topped the Amazon Comedy Book Charts! He was recently named one of the Most Inspiring Immigrants in Atlantic Canada and earlier this year released New Brunswick’s first ever national sitcom about, you guessed it, a British comedian who accidentally moves to New Brunswick! He loves living in the Maritimes so much that he founded the national magazine [EDIT] to celebrate and highlight the east coast to the rest of Canada: www.maritimeedit.com        “A great stand up.” Jimmy Carr  “James Mullinger masterfully straddles the line between the objective and inclusive, culturally and geographically. He gently pokes us with a stick while being one of us.” Jonathan Torrens  “James Mullinger is Britain’s greatest gift to Canadian comedy.” Stuart Nulman, Montreal Times  Book now, this will sell out!  "
      }
    ],
